WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.159
Unsupported software is difficult to defend because fixes may no longer be available.

2
00:00:05.159 --> 00:00:12.702
Payment applications should avoid relying on end-of-life frameworks, runtimes, plugins, or server components.

3
00:00:12.702 --> 00:00:15.146
Dependency management starts with inventory.

4
00:00:15.146 --> 00:00:23.268
Teams need to know which components are used, where they run, and whether they affect the cardholder data environment or connected payment workflows.

5
00:00:23.268 --> 00:00:32.168
Supply chain risk includes malicious packages, compromised build tools, untrusted container images, and vulnerable third-party components.

6
00:00:32.168 --> 00:00:38.075
Payment teams should treat build and dependency sources as part of the application security boundary.

7
00:00:38.075 --> 00:00:45.808
Vulnerable libraries should be evaluated based on exposure, exploitability, compensating controls, and business impact.

8
00:00:45.808 --> 00:00:50.477
Patch discipline needs enough testing support to avoid delaying critical fixes.

9
00:00:50.477 --> 00:00:53.311
Maintain software inventory and ownership.

10
00:00:53.311 --> 00:00:56.544
Use dependency scanning and vulnerability monitoring.

11
00:00:56.544 --> 00:01:01.274
Patch, upgrade, isolate, or replace vulnerable components promptly.

